target/
# Cargo.lock is committed: this is a cdylib with publish = false, so the lockfile is
# never seen by downstream consumers and only affects our own builds. Committing it
# keeps the 11-version CI matrix and every contributor on one dependency graph, and
# lets `cargo audit` scan what we actually build rather than a fresh resolve.

*.diff
*.exp
*.log
*.out
*.php
*.sh
junit.xml

Makefile.fragments
Makefile.objects
autom4te.cache
build
config.m4
config.h
config.h.in*
config.nice
config.status
configure
configure~
configure.ac
libtool
